1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,743
A sugar crystal hangs in thick syrup.

2
00:00:02,743 --> 00:00:04,516
Every day, it gets bigger.

3
00:00:04,917 --> 00:00:07,045
A dry bean seed sits in a jar.

4
00:00:07,045 --> 00:00:09,451
For months, it does nothing at all.

5
00:00:09,901 --> 00:00:13,488
Diya saw both in her kitchen
and asked: which one is alive?

6
00:00:13,838 --> 00:00:16,767
Most people pick the
crystal, because it grows.

7
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:18,232
Most people are wrong.

8
00:00:18,732 --> 00:00:22,780
By the end, you will know which
features truly mark life, and which ones

9
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:23,980
only look like it.

10
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:27,937
So how do biologists decide
if something is alive?

11
00:00:28,287 --> 00:00:29,899
They check five features.

12
00:00:29,899 --> 00:00:30,799
Growth.

13
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:33,882
Reproduction, which means
making more of your own kind.

14
00:00:34,332 --> 00:00:38,144
Metabolism, the chemical
reactions that run inside a body.

15
00:00:38,144 --> 00:00:41,896
Cellular organisation, which
means being built from cells.

16
00:00:42,346 --> 00:00:45,847
And response: sensing the
surroundings and reacting to them.

17
00:00:46,497 --> 00:00:48,061
But here is the catch.

18
00:00:48,061 --> 00:00:52,612
A feature only defines life if every
living thing has it, and no non living

19
00:00:52,612 --> 00:00:53,635
thing has it.

20
00:00:54,085 --> 00:00:56,552
That is what we call a defining feature.

21
00:00:57,202 --> 00:01:00,342
Let's zoom into the bean
seed, one level at a time.

22
00:01:00,692 --> 00:01:01,994
Here is the seed.

23
00:01:01,994 --> 00:01:06,291
A tough seed coat wraps two fat
cotyledons, the seed's packed lunch.

24
00:01:06,791 --> 00:01:07,691
Zoom in.

25
00:01:07,503 --> 00:01:10,637
Tucked between them is the
embryo, the baby plant.

26
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:12,727
The radicle will become the root.

27
00:01:12,727 --> 00:01:14,863
The plumule will become the shoot.

28
00:01:15,363 --> 00:01:16,336
Zoom again.

29
00:01:16,336 --> 00:01:21,284
The embryo is made of cells, each
with a nucleus and tiny mitochondria.

30
00:01:21,784 --> 00:01:23,671
Zoom into one mitochondrion.

31
00:01:23,671 --> 00:01:27,107
Here, food is slowly broken
down to release energy.

32
00:01:27,107 --> 00:01:31,681
That chemical work is metabolism, and
it never fully stops while the seed

33
00:01:31,681 --> 00:01:32,581
is alive.

34
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:35,314
Now give the seed water, and watch.

35
00:01:35,664 --> 00:01:36,564
Stage one.

36
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:39,036
The dry seed drinks water and swells.

37
00:01:39,536 --> 00:01:40,536
Stage two.

38
00:01:40,536 --> 00:01:42,236
Metabolism speeds up.

39
00:01:42,236 --> 00:01:45,188
Stored food is broken down for energy.

40
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:46,654
Stage three.

41
00:01:46,654 --> 00:01:49,211
The radicle pushes out and grows down.

42
00:01:49,711 --> 00:01:50,611
Stage four.

43
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,821
The shoot rises toward the light.

44
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:54,835
The seed was alive all along.

45
00:01:55,485 --> 00:01:56,660
Now the crystal.

46
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:59,956
It grows only when more
sugar sticks to its outside.

47
00:02:00,406 --> 00:02:04,003
Living things grow from the
inside, by making new cells.

48
00:02:04,003 --> 00:02:06,114
The crystal just collects layers.

49
00:02:06,764 --> 00:02:09,566
Let's test the five
features, one at a time.

50
00:02:09,916 --> 00:02:10,816
Growth.

51
00:02:10,625 --> 00:02:12,332
The crystal grows too.

52
00:02:12,332 --> 00:02:14,866
So growth alone cannot define life.

53
00:02:15,616 --> 00:02:16,616
Reproduction.

54
00:02:16,616 --> 00:02:19,127
Some living things never make young.

55
00:02:19,127 --> 00:02:21,951
So reproduction cannot define life either.

56
00:02:22,701 --> 00:02:23,633
Metabolism.

57
00:02:23,633 --> 00:02:27,874
Every living thing runs it,
and no non living object does.

58
00:02:27,874 --> 00:02:29,154
That one holds.

59
00:02:29,904 --> 00:02:31,400
Cellular organisation.

60
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,066
Every living thing is built from cells.

61
00:02:34,066 --> 00:02:35,633
The crystal has none.

62
00:02:36,383 --> 00:02:37,283
Response.

63
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:41,772
All living things sense their
surroundings and react, from bacteria to

64
00:02:41,772 --> 00:02:42,672
trees.

65
00:02:43,171 --> 00:02:44,941
Put the two side by side.

66
00:02:45,291 --> 00:02:49,998
The crystal grows, but has no cells,
no metabolism, and no response.

67
00:02:50,448 --> 00:02:54,878
The seed sits still, but its cells
are alive, and its metabolism keeps

68
00:02:54,878 --> 00:02:56,423
running, very slowly.

69
00:02:57,023 --> 00:02:57,923
Your turn.

70
00:02:57,914 --> 00:03:00,966
Which feature proves
the still seed is alive?

71
00:03:00,966 --> 00:03:02,636
Growth, or metabolism?

72
00:03:02,636 --> 00:03:03,947
Pause and decide.

73
00:03:07,147 --> 00:03:08,047
Metabolism!

74
00:03:08,005 --> 00:03:12,834
The seed is not growing yet, but its
cells are still doing chemical work.

75
00:03:12,834 --> 00:03:14,470
The crystal never does.

76
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,288
Remember this.

77
00:03:16,288 --> 00:03:17,914
Growth can fool you.

78
00:03:17,914 --> 00:03:19,976
Metabolism and cells cannot.

79
00:03:20,576 --> 00:03:23,685
So biologists describe
living things this way.

80
00:03:24,035 --> 00:03:28,944
Living things make copies of themselves,
change over generations, and control

81
00:03:28,944 --> 00:03:30,801
what goes on inside them.

82
00:03:31,251 --> 00:03:34,724
And they keep sensing and
responding to the world around them.

83
00:03:35,374 --> 00:03:36,937
Now, a worked example.

84
00:03:36,937 --> 00:03:39,600
Let's check four things
with the same tests.

85
00:03:39,950 --> 00:03:41,267
A sugar crystal.

86
00:03:41,267 --> 00:03:44,854
It grows, but it has no
cells and no metabolism.

87
00:03:44,854 --> 00:03:45,839
Not living.

88
00:03:46,289 --> 00:03:47,276
A dry seed.

89
00:03:47,276 --> 00:03:49,230
Cells, and slow metabolism.

90
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:50,130
Living.

91
00:03:50,345 --> 00:03:51,580
A candle flame.

92
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:54,824
It grows and uses air,
but it has no cells.

93
00:03:54,824 --> 00:03:55,787
Not living.

94
00:03:56,287 --> 00:03:57,826
Yeast in bread dough.

95
00:03:57,826 --> 00:04:01,365
One cell, busy metabolism,
and it makes more yeast.

96
00:04:01,365 --> 00:04:02,265
Living.

97
00:04:02,675 --> 00:04:04,141
Now, the exam trap.

98
00:04:04,491 --> 00:04:07,599
Many students write:
anything that grows is alive.

99
00:04:07,999 --> 00:04:12,604
But crystals, sand mounds and even
mountains grow, by adding material on

100
00:04:12,604 --> 00:04:13,581
the outside.

101
00:04:13,581 --> 00:04:15,959
Living things grow from the inside.

102
00:04:16,609 --> 00:04:17,992
Where is this asked?

103
00:04:17,992 --> 00:04:22,279
As statement questions: which feature
is a defining property of life, and

104
00:04:22,279 --> 00:04:23,281
which is not.

105
00:04:23,881 --> 00:04:25,098
Exam level now.

106
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:26,893
Read the four statements.

107
00:04:26,893 --> 00:04:28,584
Which ones are correct?

108
00:04:28,584 --> 00:04:29,853
Pause and solve.

109
00:04:35,253 --> 00:04:36,525
The answer is A.

110
00:04:36,525 --> 00:04:38,241
Statements two and three.

111
00:04:38,741 --> 00:04:39,909
One is wrong.

112
00:04:39,909 --> 00:04:44,126
Non living crystals grow too,
so growth cannot define life.

113
00:04:44,626 --> 00:04:45,844
Four is wrong.

114
00:04:45,844 --> 00:04:50,115
A dry seed is alive, so its
metabolism runs, only slowly.

115
00:04:50,716 --> 00:04:52,176
Here is your recap.

116
00:04:52,176 --> 00:04:53,677
Screenshot this card.

117
00:04:56,877 --> 00:04:59,714
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

118
00:05:00,114 --> 00:05:01,014
One.

119
00:05:00,663 --> 00:05:03,937
Why is growth not a
defining feature of life?

120
00:05:04,837 --> 00:05:05,737
Two.

121
00:05:05,383 --> 00:05:08,040
What is going on inside a dry seed?

122
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:09,840
Three.

123
00:05:09,556 --> 00:05:11,849
Why is a candle flame not alive?

124
00:05:12,949 --> 00:05:16,751
Next time: a mule never has
babies, yet it is alive.

125
00:05:16,751 --> 00:05:17,651
How?

126
00:05:17,274 --> 00:05:22,142
We find out in growth, reproduction,
metabolism and cellular organisation.
